  "id": "santo_daime_hinarios",
  "name": "Santo Daime hinários (Acre ayahuasca hymnody)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Hymn repertoire of the Santo Daime religion, founded in Rio Branco, Acre, by Raimundo Irineu Serra (Mestre Irineu), whose hinário O Cruzeiro is its foundational hymnal. In rituals called trabalhos participants drink the daime brew and sing whole hinários in unison for hours, standing in formation and dancing a simple bailado in march, waltz and mazurka rhythms while shaking maracás; guitars and other instruments often accompany. The hinários of Padrinho Sebastião spread the church across Brazil and abroad.",
